// A cap on concurrently open PRs: a coding agent may hold at most 3 open
// pull requests at once. A new open is allowed only while fewer than 3
// are open, measured as opens minus completed reviews in the 24h window;
// the guard runs before the new PR lands, so `< 3` now means at most 3
// open afterwards.
//
// The `-` between the two counts is the arithmetic this bundle exists to
// exercise. Without it only the exact comparison `reviewed < opened` is
// writable, and the cap constant has nowhere to go.
//
// Both counts match `response` events (successful opens and completed
// reviews), not requests. A denied open attempt stays in the trace, so
// counting requests would let denials consume the cap.

@id("cap_open_agent_prs_windowed")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Repo::Action::"OpenPullRequest",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Repo::Action::"OpenPullRequest"::response{} && tp(t))
    ))
    - (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Repo::Action::"CompleteReview"::response{} && tp(t))
    )) < 3
};
